  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "That combined activation places an extremely huge demand on primeval essence. In Fang Yuan’s previous life the same four used the killer move to capture Kong Ri Tian, then fell soon after when a rank three Gu Master killed them while they lacked essence.",
        "chapters": [
          353
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "char_kong_ri_tian",
          "sys_gu_master"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Four chains extend from nowhere, bind his limbs, and drag him into the void. He reappears in the bronze hall, where the four old-timers stand at north, south, east, and west and activate Infinite Search and Lock. Without the fixed star Gu planted on him, the move would have no target. Once locked, his Gu worms are sealed and he cannot use primeval essence; even rank five warp Gu stays sealed. Infinite Search and Lock is both a space path and seal path killer move.",
        "chapters": [
          398
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "capture-at-the-bronze-hall",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "move_infinite_search_and_lock",
